## Phase Deliverables
The Fixer phase must produce:
- `/testcase/model_patch.diff` (required)

## Success Criteria
- Patch applies cleanly to base commit
- Patched code compiles without errors
- `/testcase/repro.sh` does NOT trigger sanitizer error after patching
- Patch is minimal (only fixes vulnerability)

## Decomposition Instructions

Break down the fix phase into these worker subtasks:

### Subtask 1: Analyze Root Cause
- Understand WHY the vulnerability exists
- Identify which files need to be fixed
- Locate vulnerable code sections

### Subtask 2: Review Candidate Fix Commits
- For each candidate commit, run `git show <commit_hash>`
- If `fatal: bad object`, try `curl <commit_url>.diff`
- Identify most relevant changes
- Skip commits that match base_commit_hash (vulnerable version)
- Focus on changes to files relevant to vulnerability

### Subtask 3: Create Patch File
- If using candidate fix: `git show --format= --patch <commit_hash> > /testcase/model_patch.diff`
- If creating own fix: make changes, then `git add <files> && git diff --cached --no-color > /testcase/model_patch.diff`
- Review patch - remove unnecessary changes (tests, docs, config)
- Keep patch AS CONCISE AS POSSIBLE

### Subtask 4: Validate Patch
- Reset to base commit: `git reset --hard $(cat /testcase/base_commit_hash)`
- Check patch format: `git apply --check /testcase/model_patch.diff`
- Apply patch: `git apply /testcase/model_patch.diff`
- Rebuild: `/src/build.sh`
- Test fix: `/testcase/repro.sh` should NOT trigger sanitizer error

